                    {
                        "form_id": "6ac30370-e5cc-414d-a84e-0697b6a5359c",
                        "entry_id": "3a07c959-8f8b-3d4e-9637-47608db2029f",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "hoked"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "078d3e02-83d7-3f1c-8685-550e9342cf39",
                        "entry_id": "3a07c959-8f8b-3d4e-9637-47608db2029f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To ascribe a false or artificial quality to; to pretend falsely to have some quality or to be doing something, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7b9f51c-fb70-477d-a15b-2a4f8641c415",
                                "sense_id": "078d3e02-83d7-3f1c-8685-550e9342cf39",
                                "text": "Sewell an anti-Semite? Nonsense. It suited Humboldt to hoke that up."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9fc9b4ef-6667-4463-af7e-f992326705da",
                                "sense_id": "078d3e02-83d7-3f1c-8685-550e9342cf39",
                                "text": "He even checked the Thomas Cooke & Son travel people about how to get to the East End (here he was hoking a bit), learning that they were ready to advise him on how to journey to any point in the world except the East End. Then he hailed a cab and found (here he was hoking further) that the cab driver didn't know how to get there either."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "206ada4d-ec13-4e39-a105-768fb306600a",
                                "sense_id": "078d3e02-83d7-3f1c-8685-550e9342cf39",
                                "text": "If we define partitions of alternative cases by means of ingeniously hoked-up properties, we can get the principle to say almost anything we like."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3649191-026f-4633-85ce-af2ea79c8824",
                                "sense_id": "078d3e02-83d7-3f1c-8685-550e9342cf39",
                                "text": "If it be asked how we come to talk about them, the answer is: for purposes of rejecting these misbegotten creatures of sophistic imaginations, “hoked up” with such things as interest, strength, and the like, which do exist, although only outside of these combinations."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
